#: ../E/turn.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Return value: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"
msgstr "Valore restituito: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/aim.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zero if everything is OK, a value different from zero if the rotation could not be performed: \n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The gun has now got the desired orientation\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>rotation impossible"
msgstr ""
"Zero se la rotazione riesce, un valore diverso da zero se è impossibile: \n"
"<code>== 0 </code>il cannone ha raggiunto l’orientamento richiesto\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>rotazione impossibile"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/array.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arrays"
msgstr "Array"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An array is basically a collection of variables of the same type or class. "
"You can use N dimensionnal arrays in the CBOT language. Each dimension is "
"limited to 9999 elements. You must use square brackets <code>[]</code> after"
" the type name or the variable name to declare an array."
msgstr ""
"Un array è una raccolta di variabili dello stesso tipo o della stessa "
"classe. CBOT consente array a N dimensioni, ciascuna limitata a 9999 "
"elementi. Per dichiararli, aggiungi parentesi quadre <code>[]</code> dopo il"
" tipo o il nome della variabile."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Actually when the CBOT interpreter encounters an array declaration, it just "
"creates a <code><a cbot|null>null</a></code> <a cbot|pointer>reference</a>:"
msgstr ""
"Quando incontra una dichiarazione di array, l’interprete CBOT crea "
"inizialmente solo un <a cbot|pointer>riferimento</a> <code><a "
"cbot|null>null</a></code>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "int a[5];  // a is now a null reference"
msgstr "int a[5];  // a is now a null reference"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As soon as you put values into the array, the elements are created and the "
"reference is initialized:"
msgstr ""
"Quando inserisci valori nell’array, vengono creati gli elementi e "
"inizializzato il riferimento:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"a[2] = 213;  // a points to\n"
"             // 3 elements [0], [1] et [2]"
msgstr ""
"a[2] = 213;  // a points to\n"
"             // 3 elements [0], [1] et [2]"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After this operation, <code>a</code> contains a reference to the elements of"
" the array. Elements <code>[0]</code> and <code>[1]</code> are created but "
"not initialized because an array cannot contain empty elements. The <code><a"
" cbot|sizeof>sizeof</a></code> instruction allows you to obtain the number "
"of elements contained in an array."
msgstr ""
"Dopo questa operazione <code>a</code> contiene un riferimento agli elementi "
"dell’array. Gli elementi <code>[0]</code> e <code>[1]</code> vengono creati "
"ma non inizializzati, poiché l’array non può contenere elementi vuoti. "
"L’istruzione <code><a cbot|sizeof>sizeof</a></code> restituisce il numero di"
" elementi contenuti."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When an array is declared with a maximum size, the program will stop as soon"
" as there is an access beyond the maximum array size. No error is signalled "
"during compilation even if the error is obvious:"
msgstr ""
"Se l’array è dichiarato con una dimensione massima, un accesso oltre tale "
"limite interrompe il programma. L’errore non viene segnalato durante la "
"compilazione, neppure quando è evidente:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\tint a[5];\n"
"\ta[7] = 123;  // no error at compile time\n"
"\t             // but error at run time\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"\tint a[5];\n"
"\ta[7] = 123;  // no error at compile time\n"
"\t             // but error at run time\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you pass an array as parameter to a <a cbot|function>function</a>, the "
"function only receives a <a cbot|pointer>reference</a> to the array. That "
"means if you modify an array element in the function, the element of the "
"array that has been passed the function will be actuallay modified."
msgstr ""
"Se passi un array a una <a cbot|function>funzione</a>, questa riceve "
"soltanto un <a cbot|pointer>riferimento</a> all’array. Modificare un "
"elemento nella funzione modifica quindi l’array originale."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/bloc.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blocks"
msgstr "Blocchi"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use braces <code>{ }</code> to group a number of instructions "
"together in order to make one single block out of them, for example: "
msgstr ""
"Puoi racchiudere più istruzioni tra parentesi graffe <code>{ }</code> per "
"formare un unico blocco, per esempio: "

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/bloc.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t{\n"
"\t\tfloat  t;\n"
"\t\tt = a;\n"
"\t\ta = b;\n"
"\t\tb = t;  // switches round a and b\n"
"\t}"
msgstr ""
"\t{\n"
"\t\tfloat  t;\n"
"\t\tt = a;\n"
"\t\ta = b;\n"
"\t\tb = t;  // switches round a and b\n"
"\t}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every instruction in the block is followed by a <a cbot|term>semicolon</a>, but the block itself is not. \n"
"Let us take the following example with the instruction <code><a cbot|if>if</a></code> to illustrate the use of blocks in a program:"
msgstr ""
"Ogni istruzione del blocco termina con un <a cbot|term>punto e virgola</a>, il blocco stesso no. \n"
"L’esempio seguente, con <code><a cbot|if>if</a></code>, illustra l’uso dei blocchi:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/bloc.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tif ( a < b )\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 1<c/>;\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 2<c/>;\n"
"\t<n/>instruction 3<c/>;"
msgstr ""
"\tif ( a < b )\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 1<c/>;\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 2<c/>;\n"
"\t<n/>instruction 3<c/>;"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the <a cbot|cond>condition</a> is true, instructions 1, 2 and 3 are performed. If the condition is false, only instruction 1 is ignored, instructions 2 and 3 are performed. The fact that instruction 2 is lined up with instruction 1 does not matter. \n"
"If you want to perform instructions 1 and 2 only if the condition is true, you have to bracket them together in a block: "
msgstr ""
"Se la <a cbot|cond>condizione</a> è vera, vengono eseguite le istruzioni 1, 2 e 3. Se è falsa, viene saltata solo la 1: la 2 e la 3 vengono comunque eseguite. Il rientro dell’istruzione 2 non modifica questo comportamento. \n"
"Per eseguire sia la 1 sia la 2 soltanto quando la condizione è vera, racchiudile in un blocco: "

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/bloc.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tif ( a < b )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 1<c/>;\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 2<c/>;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t<n/>instruction 3<c/>;"
msgstr ""
"\tif ( a < b )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 1<c/>;\n"
"\t\t<n/>instruction 2<c/>;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t<n/>instruction 3<c/>;"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Blocks may be needed with instructions <code><a cbot|if>if</a></code>, <code><a cbot|while>while</a></code> and <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code>, in order to group several instructions that should be performed only if a condition is true, or repeated several times. \n"
"You can fit blocks into other blocks, on as many levels as you need. Here is an example of imbrication on two levels :"
msgstr ""
"I blocchi servono con <code><a cbot|if>if</a></code>, <code><a cbot|while>while</a></code> e <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code> per raggruppare istruzioni condizionali o ripetute. \n"
"Puoi annidare blocchi su quanti livelli vuoi. Ecco un esempio su due livelli:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/bloc.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tif ( a > b )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tint  i = 0;\n"
"\t\twhile ( i < 18 )\n"
"\t\t{\n"
"\t\t\tmove(10);\n"
"\t\t\tturn(5);\n"
"\t\t\ti = i+1;\n"
"\t\t}\n"
"\t}"
msgstr ""
"\tif ( a > b )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tint  i = 0;\n"
"\t\twhile ( i < 18 )\n"
"\t\t{\n"
"\t\t\tmove(10);\n"
"\t\t\tturn(5);\n"
"\t\t\ti = i+1;\n"
"\t\t}\n"
"\t}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You had better line up the open brace <code>{</code> with the closing brace "
"<code>}</code> in order to improve readability, but it is not compulsory. "
"The following example takes less space, is equivalent to the previous "
"example, but it is not advisable to write your programs in the following "
"style : "
msgstr ""
"Per migliorare la leggibilità conviene allineare la parentesi graffa di "
"apertura <code>{</code> con quella di chiusura <code>}</code>, ma non è "
"obbligatorio. Il seguente esempio equivale al precedente e occupa meno "
"spazio, ma questo stile è sconsigliato: "

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/bloc.txt:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tif(a>b) { int i=0; while(i<18) {\n"
"\tmove(10);turn(5);i=i+1; }}"
msgstr ""
"\tif(a>b) { int i=0; while(i<18) {\n"
"\tmove(10);turn(5);i=i+1; }}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bloc.txt:49 ../E/do.txt:28 ../E/motor.txt:39 ../E/while.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot>Instructions</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a "
"cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<a cbot>Istruzioni</a>, <a cbot|type>tipi</a> e <a "
"cbot|category>categorie</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/bool.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Type <code>bool</code>"
msgstr "Tipo <code>bool</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/bool.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a variable of this type you can put a boolean value, that is a value that"
" can take only two states: true or false. "
msgstr ""
"Una variabile di questo tipo contiene un valore booleano, che può assumere "
"soltanto due stati: vero o falso. "

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/break.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>break</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>break</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/break.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/>while ( condition )\n"
"{\n"
"\tbreak;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"<c/>while ( condition )\n"
"{\n"
"\tbreak;\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/break.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this instruction, you can get out immediately of a <code><a "
"cbot|while>while</a></code> or <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code> loop."
msgstr ""
"Questa istruzione permette di uscire immediatamente da un ciclo <code><a "
"cbot|while>while</a></code> o <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/break.txt:10 ../E/continue.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is an example:"
msgstr "Ecco un esempio:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/break.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/>int i = 0;\n"
"while ( true )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>Instructions ...<c/>\n"
"\ti = i+1;\n"
"\tif ( i >= 10 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t<n/>more instructions ...<c/>\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"<c/>int i = 0;\n"
"while ( true )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>Instructions ...<c/>\n"
"\ti = i+1;\n"
"\tif ( i >= 10 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t<n/>more instructions ...<c/>\n"
"}"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/category.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Value <code>Categories</code>"
msgstr "Valore <code>Categories</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/category.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Categories represent the names of objects in the CBOT language. Everything "
"in COLOBOT is an object: robots, buildings, raw materials, etc., even "
"yourself."
msgstr ""
"Le categorie rappresentano i nomi degli oggetti nel linguaggio CBOT. In "
"COLOBOT tutto è un oggetto: robot, edifici, materie prime e persino "
"l’astronauta."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/category.txt:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       <code><a object|titanore>TitaniumOre</a>          </code>Titanium Ore\n"
"       <code><a object|uranore>UraniumOre</a>           </code>Uranium Ore\n"
"       <code><a object|titan>Titanium</a>             </code>Cube of converted Titanium\n"
"       <code><a object|power>PowerCell</a>            </code>Regular Power Cell\n"
