#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also draw colored symbols:"
msgstr "Puoi disegnare anche simboli colorati:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/colors.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><format const>BlackArrow</format></code>\n"
"<code><format const>RedArrow</format></code>"
msgstr ""
"<code><format const>BlackArrow</format></code>\n"
"<code><format const>RedArrow</format></code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/cos.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>cos</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>cos</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/cos.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>cos ( angle );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>cos ( angle );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/cos.txt:6 ../E/sin.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle in degrees."
msgstr "Angolo in gradi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/cos.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cosine of the angle."
msgstr "Coseno dell’angolo."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/destroy.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>destroy</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>destroy</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/destroy.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/><a cbot|object>object</a>.destroy ( );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/><a cbot|object>object</a>.destroy ( );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Destroys an object."
msgstr "Distrugge un oggetto."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|destroy>Destroyer</a>."
msgstr "<a object|destroy>Distruttore</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <code>destroy()</code>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The operation of destroying of an object was started\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The instruction could not be done (e.g. nothing to destroy)"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <code>destroy()</code> restituirà un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>distruzione avviata\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>istruzione impossibile (per esempio niente da distruggere)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/detect.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>detect</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>detect</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/detect.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the instruction <c/>detect();<n/>, you can look for objects like <a "
"object|mother>enemies</a>, bots, buildings or raw materials, which are in "
"front of the bot. It is a simpler version of <c/><a "
"cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>."
msgstr ""
"Con <c/>detect();<n/> cerchi davanti al robot oggetti come <a "
"object|mother>nemici</a>, robot, edifici o materie prime. È una versione "
"semplificata di <c/><a cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/detect.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>detect ( cat );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>detect ( cat );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/detect.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Detects the nearest object of the specified <a cbot|category>category</a> "
"being in front of the bot. It is similar to the following instruction:"
msgstr ""
"Rileva l’oggetto più vicino della <a cbot|category>categoria</a> indicata "
"davanti al robot. È simile a:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/detect.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>radar(cat, 0, 45, 0, 20);<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>radar(cat, 0, 45, 0, 20);<n/>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/detect.txt:12 ../E/radar.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|category>Category</a> of the objects that should be detected. For "
"example, when you are looking for an ant, write "
"<code>radar(AlienAnt)</code>. "
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|category>Categoria</a> degli oggetti da rilevare. Per esempio, per "
"cercare una formica scrivi <code>radar(AlienAnt)</code>. "

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/detect.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> of categories of the objects that should be "
"detected. For example, when you are looking only for grabbers:<c/>"
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> delle categorie da rilevare. Per esempio, per "
"cercare soltanto robot trasportatori:<c/>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/detect.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int bots[4];\n"
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"object nearestGrabber = radar(bots);"
msgstr ""
"int bots[4];\n"
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"object nearestGrabber = radar(bots);"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/detect.txt:21 ../E/search.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keyword <format const>Any</format> if you are looking for any object "
"(including even plants and so on)."
msgstr ""
"La parola chiave <format const>Any</format> cerca qualsiasi oggetto, "
"comprese piante e simili."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/detect.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<format const>true</format> if the object was found\n"
"<format const>false</format> if the object was not found"
msgstr ""
"<format const>true</format> se l’oggetto è stato trovato\n"
"<format const>false</format> se non è stato trovato"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/factory.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>factory</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>factory</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|category>Category</a> of the robot to construct."
msgstr "<a cbot|category>Categoria</a> del robot da costruire."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/factory.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"program: <code><a cbot|string>string</a></code> (default value: "
"<code>\"\"</code>)"
msgstr ""
"program: <code><a cbot|string>string</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>\"\"</code>)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <code>factory()</code>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The construction successfully started\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The construction could not be started (e.g. no <a object|titan>Titanium</a> in the factory, the bot is not researched)"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <code>factory()</code> restituirà un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>costruzione avviata\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>impossibile avviare la costruzione (per esempio manca <a object|titan>titanio</a> nella fabbrica o il robot non è ancora ricercato)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/flatspace.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>flatspace</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>flatspace</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/flatspace.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>flatspace ( center, flatmin, rmin, rmax, dist );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>flatspace ( center, flatmin, rmin, rmax, dist );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flatspace.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determines the position of the nearest free space with at least "
"<code>flatmin</code> of flat ground around a given position. Works similar "
"to <c/><a cbot|space>space();</a><n/>. Useful for finding a place for a <a "
"cbot|category>building</a>."
msgstr ""
"Trova lo spazio libero più vicino con almeno <code>flatmin</code> di terreno"
" piano attorno al punto indicato. Funziona come <c/><a "
"cbot|space>space();</a><n/> ed è utile per trovare un sito per un <a "
"cbot|category>edificio</a>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/flatspace.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "flatmin: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "flatmin: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flatspace.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimum radius of flat ground around the desired position."
msgstr ""
"Raggio minimo di terreno pianeggiante attorno alla posizione desiderata."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/floor.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>floor</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>floor</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/floor.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>floor ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>floor ( value );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/floor.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rounds down a number."
msgstr "Arrotonda un numero verso il basso."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/floor.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Floor of the value, i.e. the largest integer not greater than "
"<code>value</code>. For example, <code>floor(2.9)</code> is "
"<code>2.00</code>."
msgstr ""
"Il massimo intero non superiore a <code>value</code>. Per esempio "
"<code>floor(2.9)</code> restituisce <code>2.00</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/for.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: count from 1 to 4\n"
"<c/><s/><c/>for ( i = 1 ; i <= 4 ; i++ )"
msgstr ""
"Esempio: conta da 1 a 4\n"
"<c/><s/><c/>for ( i = 1 ; i <= 4 ; i++ )"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function, simply put, is an instruction created by you."
msgstr "Una funzione è, in parole semplici, un’istruzione creata da te."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Main function"
msgstr "Funzione principale"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You probably already know how to create a function. Every program in CBOT "
"must have a main function, which looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Probabilmente sai già creare una funzione. Ogni programma CBOT deve avere "
"una funzione principale di questa forma:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::ProgramName()\n"
"{\n"
"\t\n"
"\t// instructions\n"
"\t\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::ProgramName()\n"
"{\n"
"\t\n"
"\t// instructions\n"
"\t\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With functions you can divide your program into several parts. Each of them "
"will execute a specific task. For example, see the following program:"
msgstr ""
"Con le funzioni puoi dividere il programma in parti, ciascuna dedicata a un "
"compito. Per esempio:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::Remote()\n"
"{\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 1, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 3, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 2, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 4, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::Remote()\n"
"{\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 1, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 3, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 2, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", 4, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|send>send</a></code> and <code><a cbot|wait>wait</a></code> "
"are repeated several times. So it would be a good thing if we created a "
"function that executes these two instructions:"
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|send>send</a></code> e <code><a cbot|wait>wait</a></code> si "
"ripetono più volte: conviene creare una funzione che le esegua entrambe:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void SendToPost(float op)\n"
"{\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", op, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Remote()\n"
"{\n"
"\tSendToPost(1);\n"
"\tSendToPost(3);\n"
"\tSendToPost(2);\n"
"\tSendToPost(4);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"void SendToPost(float op)\n"
"{\n"
"\tsend(\"order\", op, 100);\n"
"\twait(5);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Remote()\n"
"{\n"
"\tSendToPost(1);\n"
"\tSendToPost(3);\n"
"\tSendToPost(2);\n"
"\tSendToPost(4);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now the program is much easier to read. It is a good practice to split the "
"program into several functions with self-describing names."
msgstr ""
"Ora il programma è più leggibile. È buona pratica dividerlo in funzioni con "
"nomi significativi."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr "Sintassi"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"result_type FunctionName(optional_parameters)\n"
"{\n"
"\tbody\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"result_type FunctionName(optional_parameters)\n"
"{\n"
"\tbody\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Result <a cbot|type>type</a> should be <a cbot/void>void</a> if the function"
" does not give any. Body is just a set of instructions. Function name must "
"be created with the exact same rules applied to <a cbot|var>variables</a>."
msgstr ""
"Il <a cbot|type>tipo</a> del risultato deve essere <a cbot/void>void</a> se "
"la funzione non restituisce nulla. Il corpo è un insieme di istruzioni. Il "
"nome segue le stesse regole delle <a cbot|var>variabili</a>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/function.txt:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "Parametri"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "A function can have parameters:"
msgstr "Una funzione può avere parametri:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void Example(int a, float x, string s)\n"
"{\n"
"\tmessage(a);\n"
"\tmessage(x);\n"
"\tmessage(s);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"void Example(int a, float x, string s)\n"
"{\n"
"\tmessage(a);\n"
"\tmessage(x);\n"
"\tmessage(s);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The <code>Example</code> function will receive an <a cbot|int>integer</a> "
"<code>a</code>, a <a cbot|float>floating point number</a> <code>x</code> and"
" a <a cbot|string>string</a> <code>s</code>. Parameters are \"passed by "
"value\", that is the values of parameter variables in a function are copies "
"of the values the caller specified as variables. If you pass an <code><a "
"cbot|int>int</a></code> to a function, its parameter is a copy of whatever "
"value was being passed as the argument, and the function can change its "
"parameter value without affecting values in the code that invoked the "
"function."
msgstr ""
"La funzione <code>Example</code> riceve un <a cbot|int>intero</a> "
"<code>a</code>, un <a cbot|float>numero in virgola mobile</a> <code>x</code>"
" e una <a cbot|string>stringa</a> <code>s</code>. I parametri sono passati "
"per valore: contengono copie dei valori forniti dal chiamante. Passando un "
"<code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>, la funzione può modificare la propria "
"copia senza cambiare il valore nel codice chiamante."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you pass a <a cbot|class>class</a> instance or an <a cbot|array>array</a>"
" as parameter to a function, the function only receives a <a "
"cbot|pointer>reference</a> to the instance or the array. That means if you "
"modify the instance or the array in the function, the instance or the array "
"that has been specified by the caller will be actually modified."
msgstr ""
"Se passi un’istanza di <a cbot|class>classe</a> o un <a "
"cbot|array>array</a>, la funzione riceve invece un <a "
"cbot|pointer>riferimento</a>. Le modifiche effettuate al suo interno "
"riguardano quindi l’istanza o l’array originale."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/function.txt:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Result"
msgstr "Risultato"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A function can also return a result with the <code><a "
"cbot|return>return</a></code> instruction. Therefore the function must be "
"declared no longer as <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code> but as an other <a "
"cbot|type>type</a>:"
msgstr ""
"Una funzione può restituire un risultato con <code><a "
"cbot|return>return</a></code>. In questo caso dichiarala con un altro <a "
"cbot|type>tipo</a>, non <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:75
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"float Average(float a, float b)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn (a+b)/2;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tfloat value;\n"
"\tvalue = Average(2, 6);\n"
"\tmessage(value);  // will display 4\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"float Average(float a, float b)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn (a+b)/2;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tfloat value;\n"
"\tvalue = Average(2, 6);\n"
"\tmessage(value);  // will display 4\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some other examples:"
msgstr "Altri esempi:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"float Pi()\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn 3.1415;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"string Sign(float a)\n"
"{\n"
"\tif (a > 0)  return \"positive\";\n"
"\tif (a < 0)  return \"negative\";\n"
"\treturn \"null\";\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"float Pi()\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn 3.1415;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"string Sign(float a)\n"
"{\n"
"\tif (a > 0)  return \"positive\";\n"
"\tif (a < 0)  return \"negative\";\n"
"\treturn \"null\";\n"
"}"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overloading"
msgstr "Sovraccarico"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can declare several functions with the same name but different "
"parameters:"
msgstr "Puoi dichiarare più funzioni con lo stesso nome e parametri diversi:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"float Pythagoras(float a, float b)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn sqrt((a*a)+(b*b));\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"float Pythagoras(float a, float b, float c)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn sqrt((a*a)+(b*b)+(c*c));\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"float Pythagoras(float a, float b)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn sqrt((a*a)+(b*b));\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"float Pythagoras(float a, float b, float c)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn sqrt((a*a)+(b*b)+(c*c));\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"CBOT will call either the one or the other function depending on the "
"parameters passed. They must be distinguishable, i.e. you can't declare two "
"functions with the same name and parameter types in the exact same order, "
"e.g. declaring <code>int Pythagoras(float b, float a)</code> will result in "
"error. Note that result type does not matter."
msgstr ""
"CBOT sceglie quale chiamare secondo i parametri. Devono essere "
"distinguibili: due funzioni non possono avere lo stesso nome e gli stessi "
"tipi di parametri nello stesso ordine. Per esempio dichiarare <code>int "
"Pythagoras(float b, float a)</code> provoca un errore. Il tipo restituito "
"non distingue le funzioni."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "object::"
msgstr "object::"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Declaring a function as a part of the <a cbot|object>object</a> namespace "
"gives it access to <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code> <a "
"cbot|pointer>pointer</a>, in other words, to all available properties of the"
" robot which the program is run on."
msgstr ""
"Dichiarare una funzione nello spazio dei nomi <a cbot|object>object</a> le "
"dà accesso al <a cbot|pointer>riferimento</a> <code><a "
"cbot|this>this</a></code>, cioè alle proprietà del robot su cui gira il "
"programma."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void object::Example()\n"
"{\n"
"\tmessage(this.category);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"void object::Example()\n"
"{\n"
"\tmessage(this.category);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/object.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use this type for variables that contain the characteristics of an object, "
"be it a bot, a building, some raw material, an enemy, etc. Here are all "
"properties of an object: "
msgstr ""
"Usa questo tipo per variabili che descrivono un oggetto: robot, edificio, "
"materia prima, nemico e così via. Ecco tutte le proprietà: "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/object.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Also, some objects have additional methods (instructions). See them in <a "
"cbot>the main list</a> in the <c/>\"Instructions specific for some objects\""
" section."
msgstr ""
"Alcuni oggetti hanno anche metodi, cioè istruzioni aggiuntive. Vedi l’<a "
"cbot>elenco principale</a>, nella sezione <c/>«Istruzioni specifiche per "
"alcuni oggetti»."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/object.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The <n/><a cbot|category>category</a> of an object allows you to know what "
"it is, f. ex. what kind of bot, building, enemy, etc."
msgstr ""
"La <n/><a cbot|category>categoria</a> indica che cosa è l’oggetto: tipo di "
"robot, edificio, nemico e così via."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/object.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>team</code>"
msgstr "<code>team</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/object.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bot's team. Used in <a battles>code battles</a>. If the object has no "
"team assigned (e.g. in no team-based levels, the object being a resource), "
"this is equal to <code>0</code>."
msgstr ""
"Squadra del robot, usata nelle <a battles>battaglie di codice</a>. Se non "
"appartiene a una squadra, per esempio una risorsa o un oggetto in livelli "
"senza squadre, vale <code>0</code>."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/object.txt:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>velocity</code>"
msgstr "<code>velocity</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/object.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Current velocity of the object. Should be treated as a three-dimensional "
"vector."
msgstr ""
"Velocità attuale dell’oggetto, da interpretare come vettore tridimensionale."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>pencolor</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>pencolor</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>pencolor ( color );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>pencolor ( color );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The instruction <c/>pencolor();<n/> instructs the bot to change the color of"
" the pencil."
msgstr "L’istruzione <c/>pencolor();<n/> cambia il colore della matita."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:6 ../E/pendown.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"color: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> (default value: <code>Black</code>)"
msgstr ""
"color: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>Black</code>)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:7 ../E/pendown.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|colors>Color name</a>."
msgstr "<a cbot|colors>Nome del colore</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pencolor.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <c/>pencolor();<n/>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The color was changed\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The instruction did not work"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <c/>pencolor();<n/> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>colore cambiato\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>istruzione non riuscita"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/pendown.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>pendown</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>pendown</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/pendown.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>pendown ( color, width );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>pendown ( color, width );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pendown.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The instruction <c/>pendown();<n/> instructs the bot to have the pen down, "
"so it starts drawing."
msgstr "L’istruzione <c/>pendown();<n/> abbassa la penna e avvia il disegno."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/pendown.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"width: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: "
"<code>0.5</code>)"
msgstr ""
"width: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>0.5</code>)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pendown.txt:10 ../E/penwidth.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Width of the pen. The width cannot be higher than <code>1.0</code> and "
"cannot be lower than <code>0.0</code>. Passing a higher value will result in"
" the width being the highest possible and passing a lower value will result "
"in the width being the lowest possible."
msgstr ""
"Spessore della penna, fra <code>0.0</code> e <code>1.0</code>. Valori più "
"alti vengono limitati al massimo, quelli più bassi al minimo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pendown.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <c/>pendown();<n/>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The pen is now down\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The instruction did not work"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <c/>pendown();<n/> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>penna abbassata\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>istruzione non riuscita"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/penup.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>penup</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>penup</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/penup.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>penup ( );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>penup ( );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/penup.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The instruction <c/>penup();<n/> instructs the bot to have the pen up, so it"
" stops drawing. The pen is up by default, so it should be used only after "
"using <code><a cbot|pendown>pendown</a></code>."
msgstr ""
"L’istruzione <c/>penup();<n/> solleva la penna e interrompe il disegno. È "
"già sollevata inizialmente, quindi usala dopo <code><a "
"cbot|pendown>pendown</a></code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/penup.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <c/>penup();<n/>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The pen is now up\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The instruction did not work"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <c/>penup();<n/> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>penna sollevata\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>istruzione non riuscita"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/penwidth.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>penwidth</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>penwidth</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/penwidth.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>penwidth ( color );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>penwidth ( color );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/penwidth.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The instruction <c/>penwidth();<n/> instructs the bot to change the width of"
" the pencil."
msgstr "L’istruzione <c/>penwidth();<n/> cambia lo spessore della matita."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/penwidth.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "width: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "width: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/penwidth.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <c/>penwidth();<n/>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The width was changed\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The instruction did not work"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <c/>penwidth();<n/> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>spessore cambiato\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>istruzione non riuscita"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/pow.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>pow</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>pow</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/pow.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>pow ( x, y );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>pow ( x, y );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pow.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Base."
msgstr "Base."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pow.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exponent."
msgstr "Esponente."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/pow.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "x to the y (x raised to the yth power)."
msgstr "x elevato a y."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/radar.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>radar ( cat, angle, focus, min, max, sens, filter );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>radar ( cat, angle, focus, min, max, sens, filter );<n/>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/radar.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> of categories of the objects that should be "
"detected. For example, when you are looking only for grabbers:"
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> delle categorie da rilevare. Per esempio, per "
"cercare solo robot trasportatori:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:25 ../E/search.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/><s/>int bots[4];"
msgstr "<c/><s/>int bots[4];"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/radar.txt:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"object nearestGrabber = radar(bots);<n/>"
msgstr ""
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"object nearestGrabber = radar(bots);<n/>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/radar.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keyword <format const>Any</format> if you are looking for any object "
"(including even plants and so on). Filters may be useful to use with this "
"keyword."
msgstr ""
"La parola chiave <format const>Any</format> cerca qualsiasi oggetto, "
"comprese piante e simili. Può essere utile associarla a dei filtri."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"angle: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: <code>0</code>)"
msgstr ""
"angle: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>0</code>)"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"focus: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: "
"<code>360</code>)"
msgstr ""
"focus: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>360</code>)"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"min: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: <code>0</code>)"
msgstr ""
"min: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>0</code>)"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"max: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: <code>1000</code>)"
msgstr ""
"max: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>1000</code>)"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sens: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: <code>1</code>)"
msgstr ""
"sens: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (valore predefinito: "
"<code>1</code>)"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"filter: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> (default value: <code><format "
"const>FilterNone</format></code>)"
msgstr ""
"filter: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> (valore predefinito: <code><format "
"const>FilterNone</format></code>)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determines which type of objects should be detected. Especially useful in "
"use with an <a cbot|array>array</a> or <format const>Any</format>. The "
"following filters are available:"
msgstr ""
"Sceglie i tipi di oggetti da rilevare, particolarmente utile con un <a "
"cbot|array>array</a> o <format const>Any</format>. Filtri disponibili:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><format const>FilterNone</format>        </code>Detects everything (default)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterOnlyLanding</format> </code>Detects only objects being on the ground\n"
"<code><format const>FilterOnlyFlying</format>  </code>Detects only objects not being on the ground\n"
"<code><format const>FilterFriendly</format>    </code>Detects only allies (objects in the same team)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterEnemy</format>       </code>Detects only enemies (objects in an other team except neutral)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterNeutral</format>     </code>Detects only neutral objects (e.g. resources)"
msgstr ""
"<code><format const>FilterNone</format>        </code>Rileva tutto (predefinito)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterOnlyLanding</format> </code>Solo oggetti a terra\n"
"<code><format const>FilterOnlyFlying</format>  </code>Solo oggetti non a terra\n"
"<code><format const>FilterFriendly</format>    </code>Solo alleati (stessa squadra)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterEnemy</format>       </code>Solo nemici (altra squadra non neutrale)\n"
"<code><format const>FilterNeutral</format>     </code>Solo oggetti neutrali, come risorse"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last three are mainly useful in <a battles>code battles</a>. You can "
"also pass a team ID to search only for objects from a specific team. "
"Attention: you should use <format const>FilterNeutral</format> instead of "
"<code>0</code> or else it will not work."
msgstr ""
"Gli ultimi tre sono utili soprattutto nelle <a battles>battaglie di "
"codice</a>. Puoi specificare un ID di squadra per cercarne solo gli oggetti."
" Attenzione: per i neutrali usa <format const>FilterNeutral</format>, non "
"<code>0</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filters and IDs can be mixed using bitwise OR operator <code>|</code>, for "
"example <c/>radar(Any, 0, 360, 0, 1000, 1, 2 | FilterOnlyLanding);<n/> will "
"only detect an object from team <code>2</code> that is on the ground. "
"Attention: you can specify only one team ID at once, but you can specify "
"several filters at once."
msgstr ""
"Puoi combinare filtri e ID con l’OR bit a bit <code>|</code>. Per esempio "
"<c/>radar(Any, 0, 360, 0, 1000, 1, 2 | FilterOnlyLanding);<n/> rileva solo "
"oggetti a terra della squadra <code>2</code>. Puoi indicare una sola "
"squadra, ma più filtri insieme."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/rand.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>rand</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>rand</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/rand.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>rand ( );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>rand ( );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/rand.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pseudorandom number between 0 and 1 (including 0, but excluding 1)."
msgstr "Numero pseudocasuale fra 0 incluso e 1 escluso."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/research.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>research</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>research</code>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/research.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "type: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"
msgstr "type: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <code>research()</code>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>The research successfully started\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>The research could not be started (e.g. the research is disabled in the level, no power cell)"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <code>research()</code> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>ricerca avviata\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>impossibile avviarla (per esempio disabilitata nel livello o batteria assente)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/researched.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>researched</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>researched</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/researched.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>researched ( research );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>researched ( research );<n/>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/researches.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Value <code>Research names</code>"
msgstr "Valore <code>Research names</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/researches.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Research names represent the types of available researches in the CBOT "
"language. You can use them to control <a object|research>ResearchCenter</a> "
"by passing them to appropriate instructions (e.g. <a "
"cbot|research>research</a>, <a cbot|canresearch>canresearch</a>, <a "
"cbot|researched>researched</a>)."
msgstr ""
"I nomi delle ricerche rappresentano i tipi disponibili in CBOT. Passali alle"
" istruzioni appropriate, come <a cbot|research>research</a>, <a "
"cbot|canresearch>canresearch</a> e <a cbot|researched>researched</a>, per "
"controllare il <a object|research>centro di ricerca</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/researches.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a program, research names are always displayed on a <format const>red "
"background</format>. If a research name is not highlighted in red, it is "
"misspelled. Caps and lower cases should be kept as is."
msgstr ""
"Nei programmi i nomi delle ricerche sono evidenziati con <format "
"const>sfondo rosso</format>. Se non lo sono, sono scritti male. Rispetta "
"maiuscole e minuscole."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/researches.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below are the different research names available."
msgstr "Nomi delle ricerche disponibili."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/researches.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Done by <a object|research>ResearchCenter</a>:"
msgstr "Svolte dal <a object|research>centro di ricerca</a>:"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/researches.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Done by <a object|labo>AutoLab</a>:"
msgstr "Svolte dal <a object|labo>laboratorio automatico</a>:"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/researches.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Impossible to research:"
msgstr "Non ricercabili:"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/round.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>round</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>round</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/round.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>round ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>round ( value );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/round.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rounds a number."
msgstr "Arrotonda un numero."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/round.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Rounded <code>value</code>. For example, <code>round(2.5)</code> is "
"<code>3.0</code>, whereas <code>round(2.4)</code> is <code>2.0</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code>value</code> arrotondato. Per esempio <code>round(2.5)</code> "
"restituisce <code>3.0</code>, mentre <code>round(2.4)</code> restituisce "
"<code>2.0</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/round.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|trunc>trunc</a>, <a cbot|floor>floor</a>, <a cbot|ceil>ceil</a>, <a "
"cbot>programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a "
"cbot|expr>expressions</a>."
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|trunc>trunc</a>, <a cbot|floor>floor</a>, <a cbot|ceil>ceil</a>, <a "
"cbot>programmazione</a>, <a cbot|type>tipi</a> e <a "
"cbot|expr>espressioni</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/search.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Detects the object of the given category that is closest to the given "
"position. Similar to <c/><a cbot|radar>radar();</a><n/>, but can search "
"starting from the specific point instead of the actual bot's position."
msgstr ""
"Rileva l’oggetto della categoria indicata più vicino alla posizione "
"specificata. Simile a <c/><a cbot|radar>radar();</a><n/>, ma permette di "
"partire da un punto diverso dalla posizione del robot."

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/search.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|category>Category</a> of the objects that should be detected. For "
"example, when you are looking for an ant, write "
"<code>search(AlienAnt)</code>. "
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|category>Categoria</a> da rilevare. Per cercare una formica scrivi "
"<code>search(AlienAnt)</code>. "

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/search.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> of categories of the objects that should be "
"detected. For example, when you are looking only for grabbers, starting from"
" a certain point in the level:"
msgstr ""
"<a cbot|array>Array</a> delle categorie da rilevare. Per esempio, per "
"cercare soltanto robot trasportatori a partire da un punto del livello:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/search.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"point p(50, 24, 0);\n"
"object grabberNearestThePoint = search(bots, p);<n/>"
msgstr ""
"bots[0] = WheeledGrabber;\n"
"bots[1] = TrackedGrabber;\n"
"bots[2] = WingedGrabber;\n"
"bots[3] = LeggedGrabber;\n"
"point p(50, 24, 0);\n"
"object grabberNearestThePoint = search(bots, p);<n/>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/search.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"position: <code><a cbot|point>point</a></code> (default value: <code><a "
"cbot|this>this</a>.<a cbot|object>position</a></code>)"
msgstr ""
"position: <code><a cbot|point>point</a></code> (valore predefinito: <code><a"
" cbot|this>this</a>.<a cbot|object>position</a></code>)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/sin.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>sin</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>sin</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/sin.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>sin ( angle );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>sin ( angle );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/sin.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sine of the angle."
msgstr "Seno dell’angolo."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/sqrt.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>sqrt</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>sqrt</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/sqrt.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>sqrt ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>sqrt ( value );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/sqrt.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-negative number."
msgstr "Numero non negativo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/sqrt.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Square root of the value."
msgstr "Radice quadrata del valore."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/switch.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instructions <code>switch</code>, <code>case</code> and <code>default</code>"
msgstr ""
"Istruzioni <code>switch</code>, <code>case</code> e <code>default</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the instruction <code>switch() {}</code> you can execute a proper set "
"of instructions (a case) basing on some value."
msgstr ""
"Con <code>switch() {}</code> scegli quali istruzioni eseguire secondo un "
"valore."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the following <a cbot|function>function</a>: the bot will be <a "
"cbot|wait>waiting</a> a proper amount of time for a certain task to be "
"completed:"
msgstr ""
"In questa <a cbot|function>funzione</a> il robot <a cbot|wait>attende</a> il"
" tempo necessario a completare un compito:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/switch.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public void WaitForTaskCompleted(object building)\n"
"{\n"
"\tint cat = building.category;\n"
"\t<a cbot|if>if</a> (cat == Converter) wait(15);\n"
"\telse if (cat == BotFactory) wait(15);\n"
"\telse if (cat == PowerPlant) wait(12);\n"
"\telse message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public void WaitForTaskCompleted(object building)\n"
"{\n"
"\tint cat = building.category;\n"
"\t<a cbot|if>if</a> (cat == Converter) wait(15);\n"
"\telse if (cat == BotFactory) wait(15);\n"
"\telse if (cat == PowerPlant) wait(12);\n"
"\telse message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This function can be also written using the <code>switch() {}</code> "
"instruction:"
msgstr "Puoi riscriverla con <code>switch() {}</code>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/switch.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public void WaitForTaskCompleted(object building)\n"
"{\n"
"\tswitch (building.category)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcase Converter: wait(15); break;\n"
"\t\tcase BotFactory: wait(15); break;\n"
"\t\tcase PowerPlant: wait(12); break;\n"
"\t\tdefault: message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public void WaitForTaskCompleted(object building)\n"
"{\n"
"\tswitch (building.category)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcase Converter: wait(15); break;\n"
"\t\tcase BotFactory: wait(15); break;\n"
"\t\tcase PowerPlant: wait(12); break;\n"
"\t\tdefault: message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Which way to write this kind of choice structures, is a matter of taste."
msgstr "La scelta fra queste strutture dipende dalle preferenze personali."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also make cases like this:"
msgstr "Puoi anche raggruppare i casi così:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/switch.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"switch (building.category)\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase Converter:\n"
"\tcase BotFactory:\n"
"\t\twait(15); break;\n"
"\tcase PowerPlant: wait(12); break;\n"
"\tdefault: message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"switch (building.category)\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase Converter:\n"
"\tcase BotFactory:\n"
"\t\twait(15); break;\n"
"\tcase PowerPlant: wait(12); break;\n"
"\tdefault: message(\"Undefined wait time\", DisplayError);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a object|convert>Converter</a> and <a object|factory>bot factory</a> have "
"the same waiting time, so in order to not write the same instructions twice,"
" we made multiple cases run the same code. In fact, all code after the "
"highest case used will be executed if we do not <code><a "
"cbot|break>break</a></code> it."
msgstr ""
"Il <a object|convert>convertitore</a> e la <a object|factory>fabbrica di "
"robot</a> hanno lo stesso tempo di attesa: più casi possono quindi eseguire "
"lo stesso codice. In assenza di <code><a cbot|break>break</a></code>, "
"l’esecuzione continua attraverso tutti i casi successivi."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/switch.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/>switch ( value )\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase value1: instructions1\n"
"\tcase value2: instructions2\n"
"\t...\n"
"\tcase valueN: instructionsN\n"
"\tdefault: instructionsDefault\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"<c/>switch ( value )\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase value1: instructions1\n"
"\tcase value2: instructions2\n"
"\t...\n"
"\tcase valueN: instructionsN\n"
"\tdefault: instructionsDefault\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this conditional structure you can execute <code>instructions1</code> "
"or <code>instructions2</code> ... or <code>instructionsN</code> or "
"<code>instructionsDefault</code> depending on the <code>value</code>."
msgstr ""
"Esegue <code>instructions1</code>, <code>instructions2</code>, fino a "
"<code>instructionsN</code> oppure <code>instructionsDefault</code> secondo "
"<code>value</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the <code>value</code> is equal to <code>value1</code>, <code>instructions1</code> to <code>N</code> (including <code>instructionsDefault</code>) are executed.\n"
"If the <code>value</code> is equal to <code>value2</code>, <code>instructions2</code> to <code>N</code> (including <code>instructionsDefault</code>) are executed.\n"
"And so on.\n"
"If the <code>value</code> is equal to <code>valueN</code>, <code>instructionsN</code> and <code>instructionsDefault</code> are executed.\n"
"If the <code>value</code> is not equal to any value in the given cases, <code>instructionsDefault</code> are executed."
msgstr ""
"Se <code>value</code> è uguale a <code>value1</code>, esegue da <code>instructions1</code> a <code>N</code>, comprese <code>instructionsDefault</code>.\n"
"Se <code>value</code> è uguale a <code>value2</code>, esegue da <code>instructions2</code> a <code>N</code>, comprese <code>instructionsDefault</code>.\n"
"E così via.\n"
"Se <code>value</code> è uguale a <code>valueN</code>, esegue <code>instructionsN</code> e <code>instructionsDefault</code>.\n"
"Se <code>value</code> non corrisponde ad alcun caso, esegue solo <code>instructionsDefault</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can exit from the the <code>switch() {}</code> instruction using "
"<code><a cbot|break>break</a></code>."
msgstr ""
"Per uscire da <code>switch() {}</code> usa <code><a "
"cbot|break>break</a></code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/switch.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do not put a <a cbot|term>semicolon</a> at the end of the <code>switch ( ) {"
" }</code> instruction."
msgstr ""
"Non inserire un <a cbot|term>punto e virgola</a> dopo <code>switch ( ) { "
"}</code>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/takeoff.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>takeoff</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>takeoff</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/takeoff.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <code>takeoff()</code>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>Spaceship takes off\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>Spaceship could not take off (e.g. mission is not finished yet)"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente un errore interrompe il programma. Puoi impedirlo con <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code>: <code>takeoff()</code> restituisce un valore diverso da zero in caso di errore.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>l’astronave decolla\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>decollo impossibile (per esempio missione non completata)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/tan.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>tan</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>tan</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/tan.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>tan ( angle );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>tan ( angle );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tan.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle in degrees (except multiples of 90)."
msgstr "Angolo in gradi, esclusi i multipli di 90."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tan.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tangent of the angle."
msgstr "Tangente dell’angolo."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/trunc.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>trunc</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>trunc</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/trunc.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>trunc ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>trunc ( value );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/trunc.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Truncation is a method of approximating a decimal number by dropping all "
"decimal places past a certain point without rounding. For positive numbers, "
"it works like the <c/><a cbot|floor>floor();</a><n/> function, and for "
"negative numbers, it works like the <c/><a cbot|ceil>ceil();</a><n/> "
"function. It can be said that it rounds towards zero."
msgstr ""
"Il troncamento elimina le cifre decimali senza arrotondare. Per numeri "
"positivi equivale a <c/><a cbot|floor>floor();</a><n/>, per quelli negativi "
"a <c/><a cbot|ceil>ceil();</a><n/>. Arrotonda quindi verso zero."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/trunc.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Truncated <code>value</code>. For example, <code>trunc(-2.5)</code> is "
"<code>-2.00</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code>value</code> troncato. Per esempio <code>trunc(-2.5)</code> "
"restituisce <code>-2.00</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/category.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a program, categories are always displayed like that: <format "
"const>category</format>. If a category isn't highlighted, it is misspelled. "
"Caps and lower cases should be kept as is."
msgstr ""
"Nei programmi le categorie appaiono così: <format const>categoria</format>. "
"Se non sono evidenziate, il nome è errato. Rispetta maiuscole e minuscole."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/type.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a program, the name of a type is always displayed like that: <format "
"type>type</format>. If the name of a type is not highlighted, this means "
"that the name is misspelled. Type names are always written with lower case "
"characters. Here is a list of the different types: "
msgstr ""
"Nei programmi i nomi dei tipi appaiono così: <format type>tipo</format>. Se "
"non sono evidenziati, sono scritti male. Si scrivono sempre in minuscolo. "
"Ecco i tipi disponibili: "

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/produce.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>produce</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>produce</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/produce.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>produce ( position, orientation, category, program, power );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>produce ( position, orientation, category, program, power );<n/>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/produce.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "r"
msgstr "r"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/produce.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>produce ( category, power );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>produce ( category, power );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately creates an <a cbot|category>object</a>."
msgstr "Crea immediatamente un <a cbot|category>oggetto</a>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/produce.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "orientation: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "orientation: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orientation (angle) of the object."
msgstr "Orientamento angolare dell’oggetto."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|category>Category</a> of the object."
msgstr "<a cbot|category>Categoria</a> dell’oggetto."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/produce.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "program: <code><a cbot|string>string</a></code>"
msgstr "program: <code><a cbot|string>string</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Energy level."
msgstr "Livello di energia."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/produce.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Return: <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code>"
msgstr "Risultato: <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing."
msgstr "Nulla."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/produce.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example usage"
msgstr "Esempio d’uso"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is used by <a object|mother>AlienQueen</a> to produce <a "
"object|egg>AlienEggs</a>."
msgstr ""
"È usata dalla <a object|mother>Regina aliena</a> per produrre <a "
"object|egg>uova</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where object will be created. The second syntax creates the object at the "
"current bot's position."
msgstr ""
"Posizione in cui creare l’oggetto. La seconda sintassi usa la posizione "
"attuale del robot."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/produce.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Program for the object. Will have effect only for programmable objects like "
"robots or aliens."
msgstr ""
"Programma dell’oggetto. Ha effetto solo su oggetti programmabili, come robot"
" o alieni."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expressions are used for various calculations with many different variables,"
" which return the desired result. What distinguishes them from standard "
"instructions are operators, which are described below."
msgstr ""
"Le espressioni combinano operazioni e variabili per ottenere un risultato. "
"Si distinguono dalle istruzioni ordinarie per l’uso degli operatori "
"descritti sotto."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Binary operations"
msgstr "Operazioni binarie"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that <code>a</code>, <code>b</code> can be values of declared and "
"initialized variables of types <code>t1</code> and <code>t2</code>, the "
"binary operations can be described as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Se <code>a</code> e <code>b</code> sono valori di variabili dichiarate e "
"inizializzate di tipo <code>t1</code> e <code>t2</code>, le operazioni "
"binarie si descrivono così:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>r = a op b</code>"
msgstr "<code>r = a op b</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where <code>r</code> is the result of the operation and <code>op</code> is a"
" binary operator which works with values of types <code>t1</code> and "
"<code>t2</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code>r</code> è il risultato e <code>op</code> un operatore binario "
"applicabile a valori di tipo <code>t1</code> e <code>t2</code>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order of operations"
msgstr "Ordine delle operazioni"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let <code>a op1 b op2 c</code> be a legal expression, then the following "
"rules apply:"
msgstr ""
"Data un’espressione valida <code>a op1 b op2 c</code>, valgono queste "
"regole:"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/expr.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If <code>op1 == op2</code> or <code>op1</code> is as strong as "
"<code>op2</code> or <code>op1</code> is stronger than <code>op2</code>, "
"first calculate <code>a op1 b</code> and store its result in a temporary "
"variable <code>r</code>, then calculate <code>r op2 c</code>, which is the "
"final result of the expression."
msgstr ""
"Se <code>op1 == op2</code>, oppure <code>op1</code> ha precedenza uguale a "
"<code>op2</code>, oppure <code>op1</code> ha precedenza maggiore di "
"<code>op2</code>, calcola prima <code>a op1 b</code> e conserva il risultato"
" in <code>r</code>; poi calcola <code>r op2 c</code>, risultato finale."

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/expr.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If <code>op1</code> is weaker than <code>op2</code>, first calculate <code>b"
" op2 c</code> and store its result in a temporary variable <code>r</code>, "
"then calculate <code>a op1 r</code>, which is the final result of the "
"expression."
msgstr ""
"Se <code>op1</code> ha precedenza minore di <code>op2</code>, calcola prima "
"<code>b op2 c</code> e conserva il risultato in <code>r</code>; poi calcola "
"<code>a op1 r</code>, risultato finale."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note: an operation can be made stronger by surrounding it in brackets, so "
"for example assuming that <code>op1</code> is weaker than <code>op2</code>, "
"in an expression <code>(a op1 b) op2 c</code> the <code>a op1 b</code> "
"operation will be executed first."
msgstr ""
"Le parentesi aumentano la precedenza: anche se <code>op1</code> è più debole"
" di <code>op2</code>, in <code>(a op1 b) op2 c</code> viene eseguito prima "
"<code>a op1 b</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Tip: always use brackets if you are not sure about the order of operations, "
"do not try to remember how strong are each of the operators. Generally it "
"should be fairly obvious."
msgstr ""
"Suggerimento: se hai dubbi sull’ordine, usa le parentesi invece di cercare "
"di ricordare tutte le precedenze. In genere l’ordine dovrebbe essere "
"evidente."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a complicated example, which uses arithemtic operations described below, showing how expressions are calculated:\n"
"<c/>Assume a, b, c, d, x, y, z, e are all initialized variables of type float or int. Then the following expression should be calculated the following way:\n"
"  a * b + c - d / x % (y * z) - e =\n"
"= r1 + c - d / x % (y * z) - e    = , r1 = a * b\n"
"= r2 - d / x % (y * z) - e        = , r2 = r1 + c\n"
"= r2 - r3 % (y * z) - e           = , r3 = d / x\n"
"= r2 - r3 % r4 - e                = , r4 = y * z\n"
"= r2 - r5 - e                     = , r5 = r3 % r4\n"
"= r6 - e                          = , r6 = r2 - r5\n"
"= r7                                , r7 = r6 - e\n"
"r7 is the final result of this expression."
msgstr ""
"Questo esempio complesso usa le operazioni aritmetiche descritte sotto:\n"
"<c/>Supponiamo che a, b, c, d, x, y, z, e siano variabili float o int inizializzate. L’espressione viene calcolata così:\n"
"  a * b + c - d / x % (y * z) - e =\n"
"= r1 + c - d / x % (y * z) - e    = , r1 = a * b\n"
"= r2 - d / x % (y * z) - e        = , r2 = r1 + c\n"
"= r2 - r3 % (y * z) - e           = , r3 = d / x\n"
"= r2 - r3 % r4 - e                = , r4 = y * z\n"
"= r2 - r5 - e                     = , r5 = r3 % r4\n"
"= r6 - e                          = , r6 = r2 - r5\n"
"= r7                                , r7 = r6 - e\n"
"r7 è il risultato finale dell’espressione."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assignment operator"
msgstr "Operatore di assegnazione"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>=</code> is the assignment operator. It is used to store the result of"
" an expression in a variable."
msgstr ""
"L’operatore <code>=</code> memorizza il risultato di un’espressione in una "
"variabile."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the left side of this operator there must be so called l-value and on the"
" right side - r-value. L-values are just <a cbot|var>variables</a><n/>, "
"r-values are expressions or just usual values. This makes the assignment "
"operator kind of special, because what is l-value is pretty restrictive (it "
"cannot be an expression, constant and so on, only single variable). Also, "
"the type of l-value must match the type of r-value (unless a conversion is "
"possible, for example assigning a <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> to "
"<code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>)."
msgstr ""
"A sinistra deve esserci un l-value, a destra un r-value. Gli l-value sono <a"
" cbot|var>variabili</a><n/>, gli r-value espressioni o valori. "
"L’assegnazione è particolare perché l’l-value può essere solo una variabile,"
" non un’espressione o una costante. I tipi devono coincidere, salvo "
"conversioni ammesse, come da <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> a <code><a"
" cbot|int>int</a></code>."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" float a;\n"
" float b = 2.0 * (a = 4.0); // b == 8.0"
msgstr ""
" float a;\n"
" float b = 2.0 * (a = 4.0); // b == 8.0"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example is actually really confusing, but this property is actually "
"useful, because it lets doing something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Questo esempio può confondere, ma la proprietà è utile perché permette di "
"scrivere:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" float a, b, c, d, e;\n"
" a = b = c = d = e = 1.0; // a == b == c == d == e == 1.0"
msgstr ""
" float a, b, c, d, e;\n"
" a = b = c = d = e = 1.0; // a == b == c == d == e == 1.0"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic arithmetic operations"
msgstr "Operazioni aritmetiche di base"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Binary operators below are working with fundamental number types (<code><a "
"cbot|int>int</a></code>, <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>)."
msgstr ""
"Gli operatori binari seguenti agiscono sui tipi numerici fondamentali: "
"<code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> e <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:53 ../E/expr.txt:90 ../E/expr.txt:116 ../E/expr.txt:141
#: ../E/expr.txt:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "List"
msgstr "Elenco"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Note"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/expr.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The <code>*</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>%</code> are all stronger than "
"<code>+</code> and <code>-</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code>*</code>, <code>/</code> e <code>%</code> hanno precedenza maggiore di"
" <code>+</code> e <code>-</code>."

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/expr.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result <a cbot|type>type</a> is always <code><a "
"cbot|float>float</a></code>. If <code>a</code> or <code>b</code> are of type"
" <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>, they are automatically converted to "
"<code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>. Note: this means that results of "
"intermediate calculations tends to be as precise as possible, the precision "
"is lost only during converting the final (<code><a "
"cbot|float>float</a></code>) result to <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>, for"
" example by the assignment <code>=</code> operator."
msgstr ""
"Il <a cbot|type>tipo</a> del risultato è sempre <code><a "
"cbot|float>float</a></code>. Gli operandi <code>a</code> o <code>b</code> di"
" tipo <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code> vengono convertiti automaticamente in"
" <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>. I calcoli intermedi mantengono così "
"la maggiore precisione possibile: la perdita avviene soltanto convertendo il"
" risultato finale da <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> a <code><a "
"cbot|int>int</a></code>, per esempio assegnandolo con <code>=</code>."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real life examples"
msgstr "Esempi pratici"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compound assignment operators"
msgstr "Operatori di assegnazione composta"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Besides the <code>=</code> operator for variable assignment there are "
"several compound-assignment operators."
msgstr ""
"Oltre a <code>=</code> esistono vari operatori di assegnazione composta."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The compound-assignment operators combine the <code>=</code> assignment "
"operator with another binary operator such as <code>+</code> or "
"<code>-</code>. Compound-assignment operators perform the operation "
"specified by the additional operator and then assign the result to the left "
"operand. For example, a compound-assignment expression such as"
msgstr ""
"Combinano l’assegnazione <code>=</code> con un operatore binario come "
"<code>+</code> o <code>-</code>: eseguono l’operazione aggiuntiva e "
"assegnano il risultato all’operando sinistro. Per esempio:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>lvalue += expression</code>"
msgstr "<code>lvalue += expression</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>lvalue = lvalue + expression</code>"
msgstr "<code>lvalue = lvalue + expression</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "String concatenation"
msgstr "Concatenazione di stringhe"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If at least one of the values used with the <code>+</code> operator is a <a "
"cbot|string>string</a>, then the operation of concatenation is performed. "
"The result of the operator is then a string, which is created by joining "
"end-to-end the string and the other value. If the other value is not a "
"string, then it is converted to string beforehand."
msgstr ""
"Se almeno un operando di <code>+</code> è una <a cbot|string>stringa</a>, "
"l’operazione concatena: unisce i due valori in una stringa. Se l’altro non è"
" una stringa, viene prima convertito."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tstring s = \"a\" + \"bc\";  // returns \"abc\"\n"
"\tstring s = 1 + \"bc\";    // returns \"1bc\"\n"
"\tstring s = 2.5 + \"bc\";  // returns \"2.5bc\"\n"
"\tstring s = \"a\" + true;  // returns \"atrue\""
msgstr ""
"\tstring s = \"a\" + \"bc\";  // returns \"abc\"\n"
"\tstring s = 1 + \"bc\";    // returns \"1bc\"\n"
"\tstring s = 2.5 + \"bc\";  // returns \"2.5bc\"\n"
"\tstring s = \"a\" + true;  // returns \"atrue\""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Tip: the properties of the concatenation <code>+</code> operator is useful "
"with the <a cbot|message>message();</a> function, because it does not work "
"with other types than string. An empty string can be used together with a "
"value in order to create a string, which actually can be passed to the <a "
"cbot|message>message();</a> function:"
msgstr ""
"La concatenazione <code>+</code> è utile con <a cbot|message>message();</a>,"
" che accetta solo stringhe. Unendo una stringa vuota a un valore ottieni una"
" stringa utilizzabile da <a cbot|message>message();</a>:"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prefix and postfix increment- and decrement operators"
msgstr "Operatori di incremento e decremento prefissi e postfissi"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example to increment the variable <code>a</code> you can write"
msgstr "Per incrementare <code>a</code> puoi scrivere"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>a++;<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>a++;<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "instead of"
msgstr "invece di"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>a = a + 1;<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>a = a + 1;<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:186
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The result of the operation <code>a++</code> is the value of the variable "
"<code>a</code> *before* the increment. If you use the prefix operator "
"<code>++a</code> the result of the operation is the value of the variable "
"<code>a</code> *after* the increment. The same holds for the <code>--</code>"
" decrement operator."
msgstr ""
"Il risultato di <code>a++</code> è il valore di <code>a</code> *prima* "
"dell’incremento. Con <code>++a</code> è il valore di <code>a</code> *dopo*. "
"Lo stesso vale per il decremento <code>--</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically speaking, an expression is an ordered series of operations "
"which yield a result. Operations consist of operators, which are special <a "
"cbot|function>functions</a> <code>T f(t1 x1, t2 x2, ..., tn xn)</code>, "
"where <code>xi</code> is a value of type <code>ti</code>, and <code>T</code>"
" is the result type. For example, <code>float +(float a, float b)</code> "
"returns a sum of values <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>. Note: Operators "
"are a part of the CBOT language and they cannot be defined in program. Also,"
" the operators cannot be used as usual <a cbot|function>functions</a>, they "
"need to be written using a special notation depending on the operator, for "
"example <code>a+b</code>."
msgstr ""
"Un’espressione è una sequenza ordinata di operazioni che produce un "
"risultato. Gli operatori sono particolari <a cbot|function>funzioni</a> "
"<code>T f(t1 x1, t2 x2, ..., tn xn)</code>: <code>xi</code> ha tipo "
"<code>ti</code> e <code>T</code> è il tipo restituito. Per esempio "
"<code>float +(float a, float b)</code> somma <code>a</code> e "
"<code>b</code>. Gli operatori fanno parte di CBOT e non possono essere "
"definiti dal programma né chiamati come normali <a "
"cbot|function>funzioni</a>: richiedono la loro notazione, come "
"<code>a+b</code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In nearly all operations, <a cbot>constants</a>, <a cbot|var>variables</a>, "
"<a cbot|function>functions</a> returning non-<a cbot|void>void</a> type and "
"also other operations can be used as values."
msgstr ""
"Quasi tutte le operazioni accettano come valori <a cbot>costanti</a>, <a "
"cbot|var>variabili</a>, altre operazioni e <a cbot|function>funzioni</a> che"
" restituiscono un tipo non <a cbot|void>void</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note: it may be not obvious at first, but notice that <code>=</code> is an "
"*operator* not an instruction. This mean that it can be used in the middle "
"of an other expression! The result of <code>=</code> is the value which was "
"assigned to the l-value - the result of the expression on the right. "
"Example:"
msgstr ""
"Nota: <code>=</code> è un *operatore*, non un’istruzione, e può comparire "
"dentro altre espressioni. Il risultato di <code>=</code> è il valore "
"assegnato all’l-value, cioè il risultato dell’espressione a destra. Esempio:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" float pi = 3.14;\n"
" // message(pi); // does not work\n"
" message(\"\"+pi);"
msgstr ""
" float pi = 3.14;\n"
" // message(pi); // does not work\n"
" message(\"\"+pi);"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:190
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" a = 2;\n"
" b = a++;\n"
" // now b contains 2 and a contains 3"
msgstr ""
" a = 2;\n"
" b = a++;\n"
" // now b contains 2 and a contains 3"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" a = 2;\n"
" b = ++a;\n"
" // now b contains 3 and a contains 3"
msgstr ""
" a = 2;\n"
" b = ++a;\n"
" // now b contains 3 and a contains 3"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "Logical operators"
msgstr "Operatori logici"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Logical operators work with values of type <a cbot|bool>bool</a> and they "
"always return a <a cbot|bool>bool</a>. They are mainly used in <a "
"cbot|cond>conditions</a>."
msgstr ""
"Gli operatori logici agiscono su valori <a cbot|bool>bool</a> e "
"restituiscono un <a cbot|bool>bool</a>. Sono usati soprattutto nelle <a "
"cbot|cond>condizioni</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ternary operator"
msgstr "Operatore ternario"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ternary operator is nothing more than a syntax sugar. It is also known as \"inline if\". It might be confusing at first, because its syntax is a little more complicated than other operators. It can be described as follows:\n"
"<code>(condition) ? (result when true) : (result when false)</code>\n"
"Brackets are not needed."
msgstr ""
"L’operatore ternario, detto anche «if in linea», è una forma abbreviata. La sintassi è:\n"
"<code>(condition) ? (result when true) : (result when false)</code>\n"
"Le parentesi non sono obbligatorie."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Firstly, the condition is valued and then the first result is returned if "
"the condition is true, otherwise the second result is returned."
msgstr ""
"Valuta prima la condizione e restituisce il primo risultato se è vera, "
"altrimenti il secondo."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:158 ../E/extends.txt:4 ../E/extends.txt:65 ../E/private.txt:4
#: ../E/protected.txt:4 ../E/super.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Esempio"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/expr.txt:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>float c = ((3.0 > 2.0) ? 10.0 : -10.0); // c == 10.0<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>float c = ((3.0 > 2.0) ? 10.0 : -10.0); // c == 10.0<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/cond.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A condition is a special <a cbot|expr>expression</a> that returns a <a "
"cbot|bool>boolean</a> value, that can only be either <code><a "
"cbot|true>true</a></code> or <code><a cbot|false>false</a></code>. With a "
"condition, you can choose f. ex. if the instructions in a <code><a "
"cbot|while>while</a></code> loop must be repeated again, or if the "
"instruction in a <code><a cbot|if>if</a></code> bloc must be executed."
msgstr ""
"Una condizione è un’<a cbot|expr>espressione</a> che restituisce un <a "
"cbot|bool>booleano</a>: <code><a cbot|true>true</a></code> o <code><a "
"cbot|false>false</a></code>. Decide, per esempio, se ripetere un ciclo "
"<code><a cbot|while>while</a></code> o eseguire un blocco <code><a "
"cbot|if>if</a></code>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comparison operators"
msgstr "Operatori di confronto"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Comparison operators work with values of type <a cbot|bool>float</a> and "
"they always return a <a cbot|bool>bool</a>. They are mainly used in <a "
"cbot|cond>conditions</a>."
msgstr ""
"Gli operatori di confronto agiscono su valori <a cbot|bool>float</a> e "
"restituiscono un <a cbot|bool>bool</a>. Sono usati soprattutto nelle <a "
"cbot|cond>condizioni</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:142
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>!a      </code>not <code>a</code>\n"
"<code>a && b  </code><code>a</code> and <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a || b  </code><code>a</code> or <code>b</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code>!a      </code>non <code>a</code>\n"
"<code>a && b  </code><code>a</code> e <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a || b  </code><code>a</code> oppure <code>b</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>!false        </code>returns true\n"
"<code>true && false </code>returns false \n"
"<code>true || false </code>returns true"
msgstr ""
"<code>!false        </code>restituisce true\n"
"<code>true && false </code>restituisce false \n"
"<code>true || false </code>restituisce true"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/expr.txt:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bitwise operators"
msgstr "Operatori bit a bit"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bitwise operators are similar to the logical operator, because they are "
"operating on bits (which can be only 0 or 1, conditions can have a value "
"only of false or true). So in theory, they should be working with basically "
"any type of variable, because each value in the computer must be stored as a"
" sequence of bits."
msgstr ""
"Gli operatori bit a bit somigliano a quelli logici: operano su bit, che "
"possono essere solo 0 o 1, come le condizioni sono false o true. In teoria "
"possono quindi agire su qualsiasi tipo, perché ogni valore nel computer è "
"una sequenza di bit."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>a & b  </code><code>a</code> AND <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a | b  </code><code>a</code> OR <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a ^ b  </code><code>a</code> XOR <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a >> b  </code>shift bits of <code>a</code> to the right <code>b</code> times\n"
"<code>a << b  </code>shift bits of <code>a</code> to the left <code>b</code> times"
msgstr ""
"<code>a & b  </code><code>a</code> AND <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a | b  </code><code>a</code> OR <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a ^ b  </code><code>a</code> XOR <code>b</code>\n"
"<code>a >> b  </code>sposta i bit di <code>a</code> a destra di <code>b</code> posizioni\n"
"<code>a << b  </code>sposta i bit di <code>a</code> a sinistra di <code>b</code> posizioni"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/expr.txt:172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>2 & 1         </code>returns 0\n"
"<code>2 | 1         </code>returns 3\n"
"<code>2 ^ 2         </code>returns 0\n"
"<code>2 >> 1        </code>returns 1\n"
"<code>2 << 1        </code>returns 4"
msgstr ""
"<code>2 & 1         </code>restituisce 0\n"
"<code>2 | 1         </code>restituisce 3\n"
"<code>2 ^ 2         </code>restituisce 0\n"
"<code>2 >> 1        </code>restituisce 1\n"
"<code>2 << 1        </code>restituisce 4"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int    [ ] a;   // an array of int\n"
"int    a [12];  // an array of int limited to 12 elements\n"
"string s[3];    // an array of 3 strings\n"
"float  xy[][];  // a 2 dimensionnal array of floats"
msgstr ""
"int    [ ] a;   // an array of int\n"
"int    a [12];  // an array of int limited to 12 elements\n"
"string s[3];    // an array of 3 strings\n"
"float  xy[][];  // a 2 dimensionnal array of floats"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/array.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialization syntax"
msgstr "Sintassi di inizializzazione"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/array.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can initialize a new array using the following syntax:"
msgstr "Puoi inizializzare un nuovo array con questa sintassi:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "type arrayName[] = { value0, value1, value2, ..., valueN };"
msgstr "type arrayName[] = { value0, value1, value2, ..., valueN };"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/array.txt:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int numbers[] = { 10, 20, 30 };\n"
"MyClass objects[] = { new MyClass(1), new MyClass(2) };"
msgstr ""
"int numbers[] = { 10, 20, 30 };\n"
"MyClass objects[] = { new MyClass(1), new MyClass(2) };"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the instruction <c/>radar();<n/>, you can look for objects like <a "
"object|mother>enemies</a>, bots, buildings or raw materials."
msgstr ""
"Con <c/>radar();<n/> cerchi oggetti come <a object|mother>nemici</a>, robot,"
" edifici e materie prime."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:81
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/><a cbot|radarall>radarall</a>();<n/>, <a cbot>programming</a>, <a "
"cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<c/><a cbot|radarall>radarall</a>();<n/>, <a cbot>programmazione</a>, <a "
"cbot|type>tipi</a> e <a cbot|category>categorie</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/radarall.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>radarall</code>"
msgstr "Istruzione <code>radarall</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radarall.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/>radarall();<n/> is an enhancement of the <c/><a "
"cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/> function -- it detects all objects matching the "
"given criteria."
msgstr ""
"<c/>radarall();<n/> estende <c/><a cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>: rileva tutti"
" gli oggetti che soddisfano i criteri indicati."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/radarall.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example<c/>"
msgstr "Esempio<c/>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/radarall.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>radarall ( cat, angle, focus, min, max, sens, filter );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>radarall ( cat, angle, focus, min, max, sens, filter );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radarall.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The function works generally the same as the <c/><a "
"cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/> function with the only difference being that it "
"returns an <a cbot|array>array</a> of <a cbot|object>objects</a> instead of "
"one object. If no object is found, <code><a cbot|null>null</a></code> is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Funziona come <c/><a cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>, ma restituisce un <a "
"cbot|array>array</a> di <a cbot|object>oggetti</a> anziché uno solo. Se non "
"trova nulla restituisce <code><a cbot|null>null</a></code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radarall.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The order of objects in the returned array is sorted by distance and depends"
" on the <code>sens</code> parameter. The first object in the array is the "
"object which would be returned by the <c/>radar();<n/> function called with "
"the exactly same parameters."
msgstr ""
"L’array è ordinato per distanza secondo <code>sens</code>. Il primo elemento"
" è quello che <c/>radar();<n/> restituirebbe con gli stessi parametri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radarall.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/><a cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>, <a cbot>programming</a>, <a "
"cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<c/><a cbot|radar>radar</a>();<n/>, <a cbot>programmazione</a>, <a "
"cbot|type>tipi</a> e <a cbot|category>categorie</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/for.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "This set of instructions is executed before the first loop instance."
msgstr "Queste istruzioni vengono eseguite prima della prima iterazione."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/for.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This set of instructions is executed at the end of every instance of the "
"loop. "
msgstr "Queste istruzioni vengono eseguite alla fine di ogni iterazione. "

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/for.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executing more instructions"
msgstr "Eseguire più istruzioni"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/for.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the <code>before</code> and <code>end</code> part of a <code>for</code> "
"loop you can specify more than one instruction by using comma. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Nelle parti <code>before</code> ed <code>end</code> di un ciclo "
"<code>for</code> puoi inserire più istruzioni separate da virgole. Esempio:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/for.txt:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int i = 0;\n"
"int j;\n"
"for (i++, j = 2; i < 3 && j > 0; i++, j--)\n"
"{\n"
"    message(i);\n"
"    message(j);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"int i = 0;\n"
"int j;\n"
"for (i++, j = 2; i < 3 && j > 0; i++, j--)\n"
"{\n"
"    message(i);\n"
"    message(j);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/for.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output of the above code is <code>1 2 2 1</code>."
msgstr "L’output del codice precedente è <code>1 2 2 1</code>."

#. type: Source code
